#{[17592186445830 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445830 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445830 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445830 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}2y\\,dy\\,dx.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445830 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd9da944-934f-55d2-b2c0-f2a5f1dc8cbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445830 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}2y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}2y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{y}^{2}]_{{x}^{2}}^{2-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((2-x)^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}-4x+4)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}-4x+4)\\,dx & =-{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}-2+4-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
